//! The `caret-shape` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property sets the shape
//! of the insertion caret, the visible marker that appears in editable elements to indicate where
//! the next character will be inserted or deleted.
//!
//! Initial: auto. Inherited: yes.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - auto: The default value. The browser determines the caret shape. This typically follows
//! platform conventions and may change based on context.
//! - bar: The caret appears as a thin vertical line at the insertion point, positioned between
//! characters rather than over them.
//! - block: The caret appears as a rectangle that overlaps the next character after the insertion
//! point. If no character follows, it appears after the last character.
//! - underscore: The caret appears as a thin horizontal line underneath the next character after the
//! insertion point. If no character follows, it appears after the last character.
//!
//! Grammar: auto | bar | block | underscore
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-ui-4/#propdef-caret-shape
//!
//! Author guide: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/caret-shape
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

